const twoWorldsComparison = {
  gold: [
    'Owning or working family land as the main livelihood means your income depends on rainfall, soil, crop prices at harvest time, and how much of your produce actually sells at MSP (Minimum Support Price) versus the open market — most Indian farmers sell most crops in the open market, not at MSP.',
    'About 86% of Indian farm households operate less than 2 hectares of land, according to the last Agriculture Census, which caps how much a single harvest can realistically earn no matter how skilled the farmer is.',
