  <p>
    The practical response is the same one that works across most fields under AI pressure: pair core agriculture
    domain knowledge with a data, precision-farming, or agri-fintech skill layer. People who can read a satellite
    yield-estimation dashboard and also explain what it means to a farmer or a distributor are becoming more
    valuable, not less, as these tools spread — not because AI is a threat to avoid, but because it is a workflow to
    direct.
  </p>

